Hi @clementvp,

If you want to do an extract of your full data to a CSV file, you should use our JavaScript client directly: https://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-client-js

Otherwise, you could also do you own hits widgets like so:

```js
var myHitsWidget = {
  _container: $('#myHits'),
  getConfiguration: function() {
    return {
      hitsPerPage: 500
    }
  },
  init: function() {
    // if you need some jQuery code here, do it
  },
  render: function(args) {
    var out = '';
    args.results.hits.forEach(function(hit) {
      out += '...'; // do whatever you want here, any html structure
    });
    this._container.html(html);
  }
};

search.addWidget(myHitsWidget);
```
